  "result": "Excellent! All 153 tests pass, including 13 new voucher tests. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Voucher Support Implementation\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:\n\n- Applies a fixed amount voucher (in cents) to a draft invoice\n- Stores `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Validation:\n  - **NOT_DRAFT**: Only draft invoices can have vouchers applied\n  - **VOUCHER_EXISTS**: Only one voucher per invoice\n  - **AMOUNT_INVALID**: Amount must be a positive integer\n\n- Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` function:\n  - Now returns `voucher` field (amount, or 0 if no voucher)\n  - Calculates total as: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - Total is clamped to minimum 0 (won't go negative even if voucher exceeds amount due)\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error code:\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: When trying to apply a second voucher\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Voucher application to draft invoices\n- Voucher reduction of total\n- Error conditions (duplicate voucher, non-draft invoices, invalid amounts)\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, float values)\n- Immutability verification\n- Voucher + discount interaction\n- Large voucher amounts\n- Total clamping to 0 minimum\n- Code and amount storage\n\nAll 153 tests pass (140 existing + 13 new voucher tests).",
